    pass 3 phase 1: the raw root in shadow — deals_raw / labels_raw landed by both lanes, data_gaps on the runs row, backfill
    
    Both lanes reconstructed their outputs per run (new_deals_runs, new_deals_history) but never persisted their inputs: the
    HubSpot search result was consumed by shape() and discarded, six hot-score inputs were columns of no table, lane C computed
    a TEMP table over a full-refresh sync. A past run's score, duplicates, labels and report could not be recomputed from
    BigQuery. The missing node is a run_ts-keyed root, not an orchestrator (docs/PASS3_RAW_ROOT.md, decisions of 2026-10-21).
    
    - bigquery_schema.sql: deals_raw (properties JSON as delivered, in_scope, createdate, pipeline_id, fetched_at) and labels_raw,
      keyed by (run_ts, entity, orchestrator) like new_deals_history; new_deals_runs.data_gaps ARRAY<STRING>; all IF NOT EXISTS.
    - main.py: land_raw()/land_labels() after the search and before shape() — load first, delete-older second, properties as the
      dict, never a streaming insert; non-fatal in phase 1 (raw_landing_failed in data_gaps); dry does not land; event mode lands
      its one deal with mode = 'event'; PROPS + hs_lastmodifieddate (29); write_run() takes the gaps as an ArrayQueryParameter.
    - sql/land_raw.sql: lane C lands its 90-day set from the SYNC TABLE with HubSpot property names and the labels from the synced
      views, same order; spliced into new_deals_weekly.sql at `-- @include land_raw.sql` by scheduled_query.sh (now needs
      SYNC_DEALS_TABLE), after the freshness guard and outside the transaction; the runs row carries data_gaps.
    - sql/backfill_raw.sh: one-time 90-day landing per entity with orchestrator = backfill at the cut-over run_ts.
    - tests/test_main_offline.py: FakeBQ reads the raw tables' columns from the DDL, extracts array parameters, keeps one ordered
      call list, can fail the landing; 7 new tests (order, slice replacement, JSON dict, dry, failure named, clean gaps, event).
    - docs: PASS3_RAW_ROOT.md (plan + decisions + acceptance SQL), R54 and the L4/L13 cells + one equality check in
      execution_surfaces.yaml (workbook rebuilt, verify OK), architecture nodes + tree, README item 8 + index, timeline row,
      function README, PASS1/runbook table lists.
    
    Behaviour change of a live run: two more tables written and one array column on the runs row; nothing else.
    Rollback: remove the two calls in main.py and the @include line.
    
